From: relay12 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11on12: shim the remaining SAL annotations the toolchain lacks

Patch 0018 shims _Maybenull_, which is the first annotation the WDK
overlay headers use that the pinned llvm-mingw does not define. It is
not the only one.

mingw-w64 added 137 SAL annotations in v13.0.0, and llvm-mingw 20240619
bundles an earlier release; _Maybenull_ is simply the one this build
reached first. Because an unknown annotation halts the parse where it
appears, finding them one at a time costs a full CI build per
annotation. This adds the other 136 as a set, taken as the exact
v12.0.0-to-v13.0.0 delta and each defined the way v13 defines it --
empty, with the same arity.

These carry no codegen meaning; they are static-analysis intent this
toolchain does not consume. Each is #ifndef-guarded, so a toolchain bump
that supplies them makes the block inert rather than conflicting, and
_Maybenull_ is deliberately excluded here since 0018 already defines it.

Verified: the block compiles standalone under host Clang with -Wall
-Wextra -Werror, and a use test exercises zero-, one- and two-argument
annotations in real declaration positions while pre-defining two of them
to confirm the guards make redefinition inert.
---
